# Grain v1 Stream Cipher

A C implementation project for studying the Grain v1 stream cipher.

## 1. Introduction

Grain v1 is a synchronous stream cipher designed for lightweight cryptographic applications. It generates a keystream from a secret key and an initialization vector (IV).

This project implements a basic Grain v1 program in C and runs it on Ubuntu Linux.

## 2. Project Objectives

* Study the operating principle of the Grain v1 stream cipher.
* Implement the algorithm using the C programming language.
* Generate a keystream from a key and an IV.
* Compile and run the program using GCC.
* Test the implementation against official reference test vectors.

## 3. Algorithm Overview

Grain v1 uses the following parameters:

| Parameter                  |    Size |
| -------------------------- | ------: |
| Secret key                 | 80 bits |
| Initialization vector (IV) | 64 bits |
| LFSR                       | 80 bits |
| NFSR                       | 80 bits |
| Initialization clocks      |     160 |

The cipher combines a Linear Feedback Shift Register (LFSR), a Nonlinear Feedback Shift Register (NFSR), and an output function to generate the keystream.

For encryption and decryption, the keystream is XORed with the input data.

