## 5. Requirements

* Ubuntu Linux
* GCC compiler
* GNU Make
* Visual Studio Code (optional)

Install the required build tools:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install build-essential
```

## 6. Build and Run

Open a terminal in the project directory.

Build the main program:

```bash
make
```

Run the program:

```bash
./grain
```

Run the basic test:

```bash
make test
```

Remove generated executables:

```bash
make clean
```

## 7. Testing

The current test program generates a keystream using an all-zero key and an all-zero IV.

A successful build confirms that the source code compiles. It does not, by itself, prove that the implementation conforms to the Grain v1 specification.

The output must be compared with an authoritative Grain v1 reference test vector before the implementation can be considered verified.

